A lookup takes the slot just past a table as one of its slots.
A table's slots end on sixteen bytes, so what it reads is the next object or the pool's free memory,
and a slot that reads as empty fails the call as it should:
nothing the kernel does shows the read,
which reaches outside the table all the same.
The seed slot-past-table names that slot of a table the newest object of its pool, past which the pool is free,
as the capability a call invokes and as a copy's source.
Memory safety.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the kernel reached RAM outside its objects
Report: the kernel reached outside RAM
Witness: fuzz slot-past-table

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 
